{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running an automated code generation task (stitch task #5654) to implement srd110-pr requirements R2.1, R2.2, and R2.3 in the `cmd/pr` utility. Specifically:\n   - **R2.1**: Implement `-l N` / `--length=N` (set page length to N lines) and `-h HEADER` / `--header=HEADER` (replace filename in the header)\n   - **R2.2**: Implement `-t` / `--omit-header` (suppress 5-line header and 5-line footer) and `-T` / `--omit-pagination` (suppress header/footer AND do not pad page bottom)\n   - **R2.3**: Must read from FILE arguments or stdin when no file or `\"-\"` is given (partially exists already)\n   \n   Acceptance criteria require: all R2.x requirements implemented, `go build` succeeds, `go test` passes (or skips gracefully), `go vet` reports no issues.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU `pr` utility for paginating/columnating files for printing\n   - Differential testing against Homebrew GNU `gpr` reference binary via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Page layout: default 66 lines total (5 header + 56 body + 5 footer)\n   - `-l N` changes total page length, so body = N - headerSize - footerSize\n   - `-t` removes header/footer entirely (all lines become body)\n   - `-T` removes header/footer AND stops padding the body to fill the page\n   - LC_ALL=C required in test environments\n   - 40-line function limit, 500-line file limit per execution constitution\n   - Non-goal: `-m` (merge files side by side) is NOT to be implemented\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd110-pr.yaml**\n     - Full SRD defining all requirements R1-R5 for cmd/pr\n     - R2.1: `-l N`/`--length=N` and `-h HEADER`/`--header=HEADER`\n     - R2.2: `-t`/`--omit-header` and `-T`/`--omit-pagination`\n     - R2.3: Read from FILE args or stdin\n     - Non-goals: no `-m` merge mode\n     - Package contract imports: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n\n   - **cmd/pr/main.go** (existing, needs modification)\n     - Currently implements R1.1 only (basic pagination)\n     - NO flag parsing - all args treated as filenames\n     - Constants: `bodySize = 56`, `footerSize = 5`\n     - Key functions: `run(args)`, `processFile(path, w)`, `paginate(r, filename, modTime, w)`, `readBody(scanner, n)`, `writeHeader(w, date, filename, pageNum)`, `writeBody(w, lines)`, `writeFooter(w)`\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     // Implements srd110-pr R1.1.\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"bufio\"\n         \"errors\"\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"io\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"syscall\"\n         \"time\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     const (\n         bodySize   = 56\n         footerSize = 5\n     )\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         os.Exit(run(os.Args[1:]))\n     }\n     \n     func run(args []string) int {\n         var files []string\n         for i, arg := range args {\n             if arg == \"--\" {\n                 files = append(files, args[i+1:]...)\n                 break\n             }\n             files = append(files, arg)\n         }\n         if len(files) == 0 {\n             files = []string{\"-\"}\n         }\n         w := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n         exitCode := 0\n         for _, f := range files {\n             if err := processFile(f, w); err != nil {\n                 if errors.Is(err, syscall.EPIPE) {\n                     os.Exit(0)\n                 }\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"pr: %s\\n\", err)\n                 exitCode = 1\n             }\n         }\n         if err := w.Flush(); err != nil {\n             if errors.Is(err, syscall.EPIPE) {\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             }\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"pr: %s\\n\", err)\n             exitCode = 1\n         }\n         return exitCode\n     }\n     \n     func processFile(path string, w *bufio.Writer) error {\n         var r io.Reader\n         var filename string\n         var modTime time.Time\n         if path == \"-\" {\n             r = os.Stdin\n             filename = \"\"\n             modTime = time.Now()\n         } else {\n             f, err := os.Open(path)\n             if err != nil { return err }\n             defer f.Close()\n             info, err := f.Stat()\n             if err != nil { return err }\n             r = f\n             filename = path\n             modTime = info.ModTime()\n         }\n         return paginate(r, filename, modTime, w)\n     }\n     \n     func paginate(r io.Reader, filename string, modTime time.Time, w *bufio.Writer) error {\n         scanner := bufio.NewScanner(r)\n         date := modTime.Format(\"2006-01-02 15:04\")\n         pageNum := 1\n         for {\n             lines, eof := readBody(scanner, bodySize)\n             if len(lines) == 0 && eof { break }\n             if err := writeHeader(w, date, filename, pageNum); err != nil { return err }\n             if err := writeBody(w, lines); err != nil { return err }\n             if err := writeFooter(w); err != nil { return err }\n             pageNum++\n             if eof { break }\n         }\n         return scanner.Err()\n     }\n     \n     func readBody(scanner *bufio.Scanner, n int) ([]string, bool) {\n         var lines []string\n         for range n {\n             if !scanner.Scan() { return lines, true }\n             lines = append(lines, scanner.Text())\n         }\n         return lines, false\n     }\n     \n     func writeHeader(w *bufio.Writer, date, filename string, pageNum int) error {\n         if _, err := fmt.Fprint(w, \"\\n\\n\"); err != nil { return err }\n         if _, err := fmt.Fprintf(w, \"%s  %s  Page %d\\n\", date, filename, pageNum); err != nil { return err }\n         _, err := fmt.Fprint(w, \"\\n\\n\")\n         return err\n     }\n     \n     func writeBody(w *bufio.Writer, lines []string) error {\n         for _, line := range lines {\n             if _, err := fmt.Fprintf(w, \"%s\\n\", line); err != nil { return err }\n         }\n         for range bodySize - len(lines) {\n             if _, err := fmt.Fprint(w, \"\\n\"); err != nil { return err }\n         }\n         return nil\n     }\n     \n     func writeFooter(w *bufio.Writer) error {\n         for range footerSize {\n             if _, err := fmt.Fprint(w, \"\\n\"); err != nil { return err }\n         }\n         return nil\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/pr/pr_test.go** (listed as required reading, NOT yet read)\n     - Needs to be read before adding test cases\n     - Will contain existing differential tests to extend\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (contract provided in prompt)\n     - `DiffTest` struct with Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, etc.\n     - `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` function\n     - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` for building test binary\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - only two file reads were completed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the existing `run()` function has NO flag parsing and needs significant refactoring to support -l, -h, -t, -T flags\n   - The `paginate()` function needs to accept configuration options (page length, custom header, omit-header, omit-pagination modes)\n   - R2.3 (stdin reading) is partially implemented already but needs to be verified with proper flag parsing that doesn't confuse flags with filenames\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - One massive task description message containing: role definition, repository file list, project context 