m-feed\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         use form feeds instead of newlines to separate pages\n         (by a 3-line page header with -F or a 5-line header\n         and trailer without -F)\n  \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#pr-h\u001b\\\u001b[1m-h, --header=HEADER\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         use a centered HEADER instead of filename in page header,\n         -h \"\" prints a blank line, don't use -h\"\"\n  \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#pr-i\u001b\\\u001b[1m-i[CHAR[WIDTH]], --output-tabs[=CHAR[WIDTH]]\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         replace spaces with CHARs (TABs) to tab WIDTH (8)\n  \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#pr-J\u001b\\\u001b[1m-J, --join-lines\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         merge full lines, turns off -W line truncation,\n         no column alignment, --sep-string[=STRING] sets separators\n  \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#pr-l\u001b\\\u001b[1m-l, --length=PAGE_LENGTH\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         set the page length to PAGE_LENGTH (66) lines\n         (default number of lines of text 56, and with -F 63).\n         implies -t if PAGE_LENGTH <= 10\n  \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#pr-m\u001b\\\u001b[1m-m, --merge\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         print all files in parallel, one in each column,\n         truncate lines, but join lines of full length with -J\n  \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#pr-n\u001b\\\u001b[1m-n[SEP[DIGITS]], --number-lines[=SEP[DIGITS]]\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         number lines, use DIGITS (5) digits, then SEP (TAB),\n         default counting starts with 1st line of input file\n  \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#pr-N\u001b\\\u001b[1m-N, --first-line-number=NUMBER\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\n         start counting with NUMBER